WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.483
When a post is removed, you usually cannot see who
decided, why, or check it. Modeq makes moderation a public
record.

2
00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:20.842
Five GenLayer validators classify each submission, and a
majority has to agree. Fixed thresholds in the contract,
not the model, decide allow, flag or block.

3
00:00:22.342 --> 00:00:33.300
This is the public audit log: every decision Modeq has
made, readable without a wallet. Open any case to see the
exact rule that produced the verdict.

4
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.467
To try it, open the app and connect a wallet.

5
00:00:38.267 --> 00:00:41.633
Pick an example, here a spam message, and post it.

6
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:52.950
Now the app follows the transaction: your wallet signs it,
it goes to GenLayer with a link to the explorer, and the
validators vote, usually in about fifteen seconds.

7
00:00:54.050 --> 00:01:02.833
The verdict is block, for spam, with the confidence and
how many validators agreed. Fixed thresholds made that
call, not the model.

8
00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:10.767
The case is now in the public log, with the rule that
fired. It cannot be edited or removed.

9
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.509
Modeq. Content moderation you can audit, built on
GenLayer.

